===Etymology 1===
{{inh|en|enm|cotoun}}, from {{der|en|xno|cotun}}, {{der|en|fro|coton}}, from (Genoese) {{der|en|roa-oit|cotone}}, from {{der|en|ar|قُطُن|id=fabr}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈkɒt.ən/}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/ˈkɑt.ən/|[ˈkɑʔn̩]}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-cotton.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒtən|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|cot|ton}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# ''[[Gossypium]]'', a genus of plant used as a source of cotton fiber.
#* {{quote-journal
|1=en
|url=https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/pdf/10.1111/apv.172005
|year=1976
|title=Developments of Cotton Cultivation in Sinkiang
|author=Chuen-Yan David Lai
|journal=Pacific Viewpoint
|volume=17
|issue=2
|doi=10.1111/apv.172005
|page=162
|text=K'a-shih has the most extensive '''cotton'''-growing area which amounted to 950 000 ''mou'' (6.3 million ares) in 1965.
|accessdate=16 March 2022
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200630020708/https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/pdf/10.1111/apv.172005
|archivedate=30 June 2020
}}
# Any plant that encases its [[seed]] in a thin [[fiber]] that is harvested and used as a [[fabric]] or [[cloth]].
# Any fiber similar in appearance and use to ''Gossypium'' fiber.
# {{lb|en|textiles}} The [[textile]] made from the [[fiber]] [[harvest]]ed from a cotton [[plant]], especially ''Gossypium''.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1963|author={{w|Margery Allingham}}| title={{w|The China Governess}}| chapter=2| url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL2004261W| passage=Now that she had rested and had fed from the luncheon tray Mrs. Broome had just removed, she had reverted to her normal gaiety.&nbsp; She looked cool in a grey tailored '''cotton''' dress with a terracotta scarf and shoes and her hair a black silk helmet.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} An item of clothing made from cotton.
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1887|author=Harriet W. Daly|title=Digging, Squatting, and Pioneering Life in the Northern Territory of South Australia|page=34|passage=The little girls appeared, looking fresh and cool in pretty pink '''cottons''', and we two elder ones seized the opportunity of making a more elaborate toilette than usual.}}

